    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The three meals of the day",
     "texto": [
      "The three main meals are **el desayuno** (breakfast), **la comida** or **el almuerzo** (lunch), and **la cena** (dinner).\nEach meal has an equivalent verb:\n- **desayunar** → *Desayuno café con pan.* (I have coffee and bread for breakfast)\n- **comer** → *Como arroz o verdura a las dos.* (I eat / have lunch at two)\n- **cenar** → *Ceno huevos con patatas.* (I have eggs and potatoes for dinner)\n\nPhysical needs use the verb **tener**:\n- **Tengo hambre** (I am hungry).\n- **Tengo sed** (I am thirsty).\n\nWith gustar, foods take definite articles: *Me gustan **las** manzanas*."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
